            <h1 class="pageTitle">Dispute My Ticket
</h1>

    </div>

		<div  class="span">
			<h2>Ways to Respond&nbsp;</h2>
<p>You can respond to a Notice of Infraction in four ways:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Pay the full amount.</li>
<li>Ask the court about a payment plan.</li>
<li>Ask for a Mitigation Hearing.</li>
<li>Ask for a Contested Hearing.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pay Your Ticket</h2>
<p>To pay in full, visit <a href="/courts/tickets-and-payments/pay-my-ticket">Pay My Ticket</a>.&nbsp;<br />If you cannot pay in full, you may ask for a payment plan. The court may charge a fee.&nbsp;<br />To learn more, visit <a href="/courts/tickets-and-payments/i-cant-pay-my-ticket-right-now">I Can&rsquo;t Pay My Ticket Right Now</a>.&nbsp;</p>
<h2>Ask for a Hearing&nbsp;</h2>
<p>If you want to dispute your ticket, you must ask for a hearing.&nbsp;<br />You must ask within:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>30 days if the ticket was issued to you or placed on your car.</li>
<li>33 days if the ticket was mailed to you.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h2>How to Request a Hearing</h2>
<p>You can request a hearing in three ways:</p>
<p><strong>1. <a href="https://forms.cloud.microsoft/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=RR7meOtrCUCPmTWdi1T0G_TPjbZuexNNklV_rYwmMLVURUpTUjE5WDVVOFFBRzQ0WlZZU1BPTzdWTC4u&amp;route=shorturl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Online form</a>.</strong></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Fill out the <a href="https://forms.office.com/g/5P97pMyVki" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hearing Request Form</a> online. This is the easiest option if you have internet access.</span></p>
<p><strong>2. Use Your Ticket.</strong></p>
<p>On the back of your ticket:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Check the box for the hearing you want.</li>
<li>Write in your information.</li>
<li>Bring it to 600 5th Avenue, or mail it to:&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>SEATTLE MUNICIPAL COURT</strong><br /><strong>PO BOX 34987</strong><br /><strong>SEATTLE, WA 98124-4987</strong></p>
<p><strong>3. Call the Court</strong></p>
<p>Call <a href="tel: +1 (206) 684-5600">(206) 684-5600</a>.</p>
<ul>
<li>Monday&ndash;Tuesday: 8 AM-5 PM</li>
<li>Wednesday&ndash;Friday: 9 AM-5 PM&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p>Tell the representative your ticket number and the hearing type you want.&nbsp;<br />The court will mail or email you the date and time of your hearing.&nbsp;</p>
<h2>Hearing Types</h2>
<h4>Mitigation Hearing&nbsp;</h4>
<p>Choose this if you agree you broke the rule but want to explain your situation.&nbsp;<br />The decision is final. You cannot appeal.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Contested Hearing&nbsp;</h4>
<p>Choose this if you believe you did not break the rule.&nbsp;<br />You will first get a pre‑hearing settlement conference.&nbsp;<br />This is a chance to resolve the issue without a full hearing.&nbsp;<br />You may skip this step the pre-hearing and go to a trial instead. To do that, fill out the waiver form sent with your notice.&nbsp;</p>
<p>If you contest your ticket in&nbsp;<a href="https://www.seattle.gov/courts/tickets-and-payments/dispute-my-ticket/hearings-by-mail" title="Hearings by Mail"><strong>writing</strong></a>, you cannot appeal. The decision is final.</p>
<h2>Send Your Evidence</h2>
<p>If you want the judge to see photos or documents:</p>
<ul>
<li>Upload them to the <a href="https://courtrecords.seattle.gov/portal/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Public Portal</a>, or</li>
<li>Email them to <a href="mailto:CourtCalendar.SMC@seattle.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CourtCalendar.SMC@seattle.gov.</a></li>
</ul>
<p><a href="https://youtu.be/1jlEOWRsock" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="images/Departments/Court/Tickets/WrittenStatement.jpeg" width="680" height="383" class="blockImg" alt="Public Portal Written Statement" /></a></p>
<p><em>Some of the content on this website has been edited using AI tools to improve readability and plain language. All information has been reviewed and approved for use by a Seattle Municipal Court employee. &nbsp;</em></p>
